{
  "name": "Dynamic QR Attendance",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# 🔐 Dynamic QR Attendance System\n\nAutomated attendance system for Data Security lectures using short-lived QR tokens.\n\n### How it works\n\n* Professor starts an attendance session.\n* n8n generates a unique session and a QR token.\n* The QR token automatically rotates every **10 seconds**.\n* Students scan the current QR and submit their name, student ID, and email.\n* n8n validates the session and token before accepting the attendance.\n* A signed temporary ticket allows students enough time to complete the form without requiring the QR token to remain valid.\n* Duplicate attendance for the same student and session is rejected.\n* Valid attendance is recorded automatically in **Google Sheets**.\n* A professional **confirmation email** is sent to the student immediately after successful registration.\n* When the professor stops the session, all pending tickets become invalid and new submissions are rejected.\n\n### Main Components\n\n**n8n** → Automation & validation\n**Dynamic QR** → Short-lived access token\n**Google Sheets** → Attendance records\n**Gmail** → Attendance confirmation\n**HTML Pages** → Professor dashboard & student submission page\n\n### Security Concept\n\nThe QR code itself is not a permanent attendance link. Each QR contains a short-lived token that expires after 10 seconds, reducing the risk of students using an old QR code outside the classroom.\n\n> **Start → Generate → Rotate → Scan → Validate → Record → Confirm → Stop**\n",
        "height": 588,
        "width": 1036
      },
      "id": "e52b6665-e2d0-4169-9ecd-c282e3f72f1a",
      "name": "Setup Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1488,
        80
      ]
    },
